{#
  The managed block's CONTENT - the assignment lines only, never the
  sentinel markers. blockinfile owns the markers, and keeping them out of
  here is what lets the marker spelling live in one place (vars/main.yml)
  alongside the compatibility note explaining why it is what it is.

  Escape backslash FIRST, then double-quote. The order is the whole
  correctness of this line: escaping backslash second would re-escape the
  backslashes just emitted to escape the quotes, so a value containing "
  would come back out carrying a stray \. Both pam_env and systemd's
  EnvironmentFile parser read "..." with exactly these two escapes, which
  is why they are the two that are applied and the only two.

  Rendered by a lookup() in tasks/main.yml rather than by a `template`
  module, because the text is an input to blockinfile rather than a file
  of its own.
#}
{% for entry in vm_env_vars_entries %}
{{ entry.name }}="{{ entry.value | replace('\\', '\\\\') | replace('"', '\\"') }}"
{% endfor %}
